iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so it has no HTTP authority. The request would also send the reply text to `metadata.internal.example`, which is outside that grant. If you need enrichment, it has to be a separate node that holds an `http-client` handle scoped to that host.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The `requires` clause (len(text) <= 100000) holds of every input
        // this node is given, so it is not re-checked here.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // The `ensures` clauses must hold of every output. The node cannot
        // fabricate a session identity, so if the host reports non-delivery
        // or an absent session, the node traps rather than return a value
        // that violates its contract. With panic = "abort" this is a wasm
        // trap, and the nonconforming output never leaves the node.
        assert!(
            confirmation.delivered,
            "SendReply ensures delivered == true; channel reported non-delivery"
        );
        assert!(
            !confirmation.session.is_empty(),
            "SendReply ensures present(session_id); channel returned no session"
        );

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

